WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Metacognition also appears before the work begins.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.160
Planning means choosing an approach that fits the task instead of automatically using the

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.100
same strategy every time.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.035
Different tasks require different methods.

00:00:11.035 --> 00:00:14.810
Learning a concept, debugging a failure, writing a recommendation, reviewing a design,

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:18.540
and preparing for a difficult conversation all place different demands on attention,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.160
evidence, and time.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.360
Good planning starts with the outcome.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.980
What are you trying to learn, decide, produce, or improve?

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:24.980
What do you already know?

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:25.980
What is uncertain?

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:26.980
What resources will help?

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.928
How difficult is the task likely to be?

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.305
Where should you place checkpoints?

00:00:30.305 --> 00:00:33.960
These questions help allocate attention and time before momentum carries you into the

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.305
wrong approach.

00:00:35.305 --> 00:00:39.870
Strategy selection includes choosing when to use notes, examples, diagrams, checklists,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.120
experiments, retrieval practice, peer review, or a worked example.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.230
A diagram may be the right tool when relationships are confusing.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.075
A checklist may help when steps are repeatable and easy to skip.

00:00:49.075 --> 00:00:53.050
A small experiment may be better than another long debate when the issue can be tested.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.315
The practical risk is strategy autopilot.

00:00:55.315 --> 00:00:59.205
People often use the method that feels comfortable, not the method the task requires.

00:00:59.205 --> 00:01:02.840
A strong metacognitive habit is to pause and ask, what kind of problem is this?

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.000
Then choose the strategy deliberately.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.250
That small moment of planning can save hours of effort that would otherwise be spent

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.880
pushing a mismatched method harder.
